{
  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Existing evidence strongly favors RNA-based multiprofile models, with scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer/avgpool reaching ~0.65 validation accuracy, while image-only ResNet50 singleprofile is very weak (~0.21). This leaves a key uncertainty: whether the image modality is intrinsically uninformative or whether the tested image encoder is too weak. config_013 tests image-only singleprofile with imagenet_vit_l, directly comparing image representation while keeping the profile setting unchanged. If it improves substantially, it justifies later tests of image multiprofile aggregation and multimodal fusion; if it remains weak, it suggests image features are not currently useful and budget should stay focused on RNA or other design choices. This is the best next experiment because it reduces a major source of uncertainty with minimal confounding before adding aggregation or fusion complexity."
}

